<title>SWEDEN: POLL - Scania H1 profit seen lower.</title>
<headline>POLL - Scania H1 profit seen lower.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish truck maker Scania was expected to post a lower profit after financial items for the first half of 1997 of 1.43 billion crowns compared with 2.10 billion crowns a year ago, a Reuters poll showed.</p>
<p>Sales were expected to increase to 18.10 billion crowns from 17.38 billion crowns a year earlier.</p>
<p>For the full year Scania was expected to report a profit after financial items of 3.39 billion crowns against 2.71 billion crowns for the full year 1996.</p>
<p>Sales for 1997 were expected to rise to 35.86 billion crowms from the previous year's 33.73 billion crowns.</p>
<p>Scania will release its six month report on August 4.</p>
